    -v Show version number of current IRFinder.
    -h Show this usage information.
    -m RunMode. FastQ (default. Quantifies intron retention from FASTQ file);
                BAM (quantifies intron retention from a name-sorted BAM file);
                BuildRef (builds IRFinder reference from Ensembl FTP site. Requires Internet),
                BuildRefDownload (only downloads FASTA and GTF files from Ensembl FTP site, without building IRFinder reference. Requires Internet),
                BuildRefProcess (builds IRFinder reference from local FASTA and GTF files),
                BuildRefFromSTARRef (builds IRFinder reference from a local STAR reference).

Parameters for BuildRef mode:
  required:
    ftp://... A base Ensembl URL to a (gzipped) gtf file
    -r ReferenceDir: Directory should not yet exist, will be created.
  optional:
    -t Threads: The number of physical CPUs to use by IRFinder. When ommited (default), IRFinder will use all physical CPUs.
    -j INTEGER: An integer that is parsed to '--sjdbOverhang' under STAR 'genomeGenerate' mode. Default: 150.
    -e ExtraGenomeRef.fasta.gz: Typically an ERCC reference.
    -b Blacklist.bed.gz: BED of regions to be excluded from analysis.
    -R ROI.bed.gz: A non-overlapping BED file of additional Regions of Interest for read counts.

Parameters for BuildRefProcess mode:
  required:
    -r ReferenceDir. Directory should already contain EXACT files named 'genome.fa' and 'transcripts.gtf' (case-sensitive) for genome and transcriptome annotations respectively.
